│ The core issue is that the col_suffixes      │
│ argument in                                  │
│ django.db.backends.ddl_references.Columns is │
│ not being handled correctly when an opclass  │
│ is used in the Index definition.             │
│ Specifically, when an opclass (like          │
│ text_pattern_ops) is present, the            │
│ col_suffixes are incorrectly interpreted as  │
│ empty strings, leading to incorrect CREATE   │
│ INDEX statements. The fix involves ensuring  │
│ that col_suffixes is correctly populated     │
│ with the appropriate suffixes based on the   │
│ opclass.  The provided context from the      │
│ ticket highlights this issue and points to a │
│ related fix in ticket 30903.                 │
│                                              │
│ Patch:                                       │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│  # modification 1                            │
│  [file]django/db/backends/ddl_references.py  │
│  file]                                       │
│  [original]def get_columns(self, table,      │
│  columns, opclass=None):                     │
│      if opclass:                             │
│          suffixes =                          │
│  self._get_column_suffixes(opclass)          │
│          columns = [f’{col}{suffix or ''}’   │
│  for col, suffix in zip(columns, suffixes)]  │
│      return columns[/original]               │
│  [patched]def get_columns(self, table,       │
│  columns, opclass=None):                     │
│      if opclass:                             │
│          suffixes =                          │
│  self._get_column_suffixes(opclass)          │
│          columns = [f’{col}{suffix or ''}’   │
│  for col, suffix in zip(columns, suffixes)]  │
│      return columns[/patched]                │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│ Explanation:                                 │
│                                              │
│ The patch modifies the get_columns method in │
│ django/db/backends/ddl_references.py. It     │
│ ensures that when an opclass is specified,   │
│ the col_suffixes are correctly processed.    │
│ The list comprehension now correctly appends │
│ the suffix (if it exists) to the col string, │
│ ensuring that the CREATE INDEX statement     │
│ includes the appropriate column suffixes.    │
│ The or '' handles the case where a column    │
│ might not have a suffix.                     │
